headers {
  X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
  X-User-Id: {{userId}}
  Accept-Language: {{acceptLanguage}}
  X-Correlation-Id: {{$guid}}
  Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
}

docs {
  Settings (gateway and API addresses, tenant, user, page size, language) live in the Local environment —
  select it before running. Every call goes through the gateway, as a client's would.

  Every request sends the tenant and user as GM's actor headers (X-Tenant-Id, X-User-Id), so the files you upload
  belong to that tenant and only it sees them. The gateway doesn't sign callers in: it passes these headers through
  as sent. Leave tenantId empty to work in the shared "public" space.

  Every request also sends a fresh X-Correlation-Id and Idempotency-Key; Files/Upload File Again reuses Upload
  File's key to show a retry being replayed.

  Run Files in order: Upload File saves fileId, which the later requests use. The files uploaded are in sample-files/.

  Values the scripts save (fileId, retryKey) go into the Local environment as unsaved, in-memory values.
}
